  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As $\\sin \\theta=\\frac{n \\lambda}{d}$ and $\\sin \\theta$ cannot be $\\ngtr 1$\n$$\n\\therefore 1=\\frac{n \\lambda}{1.8 \\lambda}\n$$\nor $n=1.8$\nHence maximum number of possible interference maximas, $0, \\pm 1$ i.e. 3",
